        "text": "Prior/update/interval: persistence prior is June U-6 = 7.9; historical sample is Feb-Jun 2026 BLS Table A-15 values 7.9, 8.0, 8.2, 8.1, 7.9. Adjustment components: +0.03 for weaker payroll growth and downward revisions, +0.02 because U-6 was still near its recent 8.02 five-month average, and 0.00 for no clear July-specific policy or one-off shock, giving 7.9 + 0.05 = 7.95, rounded to point 8.0. For the interval, successive changes are +0.1, +0.2, -0.1, -0.2, so sigma = 0.183 percentage point and 1.28*sigma = 0.234; because four changes are a short volatility sample and household-survey components can swing, I widen by about 1.5x to roughly 0.35 point. 7.95 +/- 0.35 gives 7.60 to 8.30, rounded to an 80% interval of 7.6 to 8.3."
